WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.918
Johnathan Abram!

00:00:01.918 --> 00:00:04.671
A lotta people like to talk trash
about your teammates and the Raiders.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.964
- Oh, I ain’t goin’ for that.

00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:07.424
- Raiders fans, get outta there.

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:08.091
Root for someone else.

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:09.467
Like, root for someone who has a chance.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.511
- Hold on, somethin’ wrong
with your microphone.

00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:13.304
- Oh, s--t.

00:00:13.304 --> 00:00:14.472
Are you Johnathan Abram?

00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:15.598
- What up, everybody?

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:17.142
Lefkoe out here in Oakland.

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:20.061
We’re meeting up with Raiders
rookie Johnathan Abram.

00:00:20.061 --> 00:00:23.940
I want you to be the best teammate
in the history of the NFL.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.401
We’re gonna surprise some unsuspecting fans.

00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:30.613
They think we’re doing a documentary
about being a non-Raiders fan in Oakland.

00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:32.198
Man, so you’re a Raiders fan?

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.242
- Ex-Raider fan.
- Oh, man.

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:38.329
They’re gonna talk trash about his
teammates, and we’ll see if he defends them.

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:41.624
And let’s be honest, bein’
surprised by an NFL player?

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:43.043
It’s a good surprise.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:47.047
What we don’t want surprises in
is in our home and auto insurance.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:53.595
All we want is good, reliable, quality
coverage, like the kind you get from State Farm.

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:54.512
Am I right?

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:55.180
All right.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:56.431
Let’s go Ditch the Playbook.

00:00:56.639 --> 00:00:59.225
♪♪♪

00:01:01.144 --> 00:01:03.646
♪♪♪

00:01:03.646 --> 00:01:05.231
- [Offscreen] Let’s roll
and sync all of our cameras.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:05.982
- [Clapping]

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:08.568
My guy!

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:09.444
- What it do?

00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:10.528
- How are you, my friend?

00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:11.112
- I’m good.

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:12.739
- Oh, it’s been too long.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:13.323
- Exactly.

00:01:13.323 --> 00:01:14.991
- Let’s take you to geek squad.

00:01:14.991 --> 00:01:16.159
- I’m a cameraman.

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:17.911
- You ready?
- Yeah.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:18.703
- All right.

00:01:18.703 --> 00:01:21.456
The ultimate teammate.
It is time.

00:01:21.456 --> 00:01:23.666
All right, assume your position.

00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:25.668
What do you think of Raiders fans?

00:01:25.668 --> 00:01:28.463
- Eh...they could be better.

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:31.966
- Man, Raiders fans, they’re
loyal fans, but they’re blind.

00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:33.134
Like, get outta there.

00:01:33.134 --> 00:01:33.885
Root for someone else.

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:35.220
Like, root for someone who
has a chance, you know?

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.138
And that’s coming from a Jets fan.

00:01:37.138 --> 00:01:38.473
- You’re a comedian, we’re in Oakland…

00:01:38.473 --> 00:01:39.724
- Ah. Oh, look at this.

00:01:39.724 --> 00:01:41.142
- Can I get your Raiders set?

00:01:41.142 --> 00:01:44.354
- Yeah, I was doin’ jokes, and Sebastian
Janikowski was actually in the audience.

00:01:44.354 --> 00:01:46.314
And he picked up his drink,
and he threw it at me.

00:01:46.314 --> 00:01:48.858
Then I remembered he was the kicker
for the Oakland Raiders for 20 years.

00:01:48.858 --> 00:01:50.902
So as the drink was comin’
towards me, I just went like this—

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.782
And that drink sailed 30 yards to the right.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:59.494
Missed me, missed the stage,
missed everybody completely.

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:00.954
- I’m a free-agent fan now.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.790
I was a lifelong Raider fan.
- Mmm.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.084
- December 2017 was my divorce.

00:02:06.084 --> 00:02:07.252
- What happened?

00:02:07.252 --> 00:02:09.504
- Derek Carr fumbled the
ball out the end zone.

00:02:09.504 --> 00:02:11.464
They traded my favorite player, Khalil Mack.

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.633
They gave Gruden $100 million.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.801
- Jon Gruden?

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.427
Pfft.

00:02:16.427 --> 00:02:17.762
Chucky doll, at all times.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.265
- Like, you know, like Derek Carr?

00:02:20.265 --> 00:02:23.017
Like, I mean, what is he, you know?

00:02:23.017 --> 00:02:24.435
- Are you excited for Nick Bosa?

00:02:24.435 --> 00:02:26.437
- Man, did you not see
him in that whole game?

00:02:26.437 --> 00:02:27.856
- What he do?
- He was throwin’ cats around.

00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:28.773
That line look—
- Don’t people do that?

00:02:28.773 --> 00:02:30.233
Don’t you throw people around in football?

00:02:30.233 --> 00:02:30.942
- This is true.

00:02:30.942 --> 00:02:32.152
You do throw people around in football.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:33.736
- Exactly. So he playin’ football.

00:02:33.736 --> 00:02:36.573
- Mark Sanchez, when he came, I
was excited about that, you know?

00:02:36.573 --> 00:02:37.574
- Yeah.
- And, like—

00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:39.784
- He suck. He fumbled off his
own lineman’s butt.

00:02:39.784 --> 00:02:41.035
- Michael Crabtree, he got mad at me.

00:02:41.035 --> 00:02:43.621
This a true story—at Tommy T’s,
the local comedy club here.

00:02:43.621 --> 00:02:46.875
I went up to shake his hand later, and he
missed me completely, just like how he missed

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:48.793
snapping off his route every single time.

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.340
- So you, you’ve actually—

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.926
- Who was the last great Dolphin
player in the last 20 years?

00:02:56.926 --> 00:02:59.387
- Probably Dan Marino, yeah.

00:02:59.387 --> 00:03:01.264
- Man.
- When, when was that?

00:03:01.264 --> 00:03:03.141
I think—I don’t think you were born yet.

00:03:03.141 --> 00:03:05.935
- Listen, the Miami Dolphins have
been mediocre for a very long time.

00:03:05.935 --> 00:03:07.520
- So how can you root for them?

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.813
- Because they’re at least mediocre.

00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:12.817
The Oakland Raiders are one 4-12 season away
from havin’ to put an eyepatch on the other eye,

00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:16.279
know what I’m sayin’?

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:19.657
- When’s the last time the Raiders went
to a single AFC Championship Game, man?

00:03:19.657 --> 00:03:23.244
Hold on, something wrong
with your microphone.

00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:24.495
Don’t be talkin’ s--t about the Raiders.

00:03:24.495 --> 00:03:25.330
- Is this—

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.539
- You good.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.749
- OK, cool.

00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:28.541
- Wait.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.293
- What do you think about Johnathan Abram?

00:03:30.293 --> 00:03:31.002
- Dude a heavy hitter.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:33.004
But he can’t pronounce his silent Ls.

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:35.882
- Seared salmon or seared sal-mon?

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:36.674
- Salmon.

00:03:36.674 --> 00:03:37.383
- Salmon?

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.218
- Salmon.

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.594
- Would you say that to his face?

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:41.471
- I’m—pfft.

00:03:41.471 --> 00:03:41.888
I don’t know.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.389
- Really?
I might. I might. I don’t know!

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.140
Look, look.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:45.892
I’mma be like this: I’m
not a football player.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:47.644
- S--t, I used to be in the
club with Charles Woodson.

00:03:47.644 --> 00:03:48.811
Sweet Jimmie’s and, and—

00:03:48.811 --> 00:03:49.395
- Old 24.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:50.855
- And Geoffrey’s and everything.

00:03:50.855 --> 00:03:52.273
- You know who wears 24 now?

00:03:52.273 --> 00:03:53.942
- Yeah, the youngster. Abrams.

00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:55.276
- Yeah.
- He bangin’ out there.

00:03:55.276 --> 00:03:56.486
- Yeah, he is.
- He, he doin’—

00:03:56.486 --> 00:03:58.905
- He’s bangin’ in here too.
- Yeah, he bangin’ out there.

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.573
- Yo, cat, you wanna go to the club with me?

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:01.658
- What?!

00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:04.452
Damn, what?!

00:04:04.452 --> 00:04:06.537
- You wanna go to the club with me?

00:04:06.537 --> 00:04:09.123
- Ah, s--t!

00:04:09.123 --> 00:04:10.166
- Salmon or sal-mon?

00:04:10.166 --> 00:04:11.292
- Listen, I’mma tell you like this—

00:04:11.292 --> 00:04:12.794
- How you say it?

00:04:12.794 --> 00:04:13.336
How you say it?

00:04:13.336 --> 00:04:13.711
How do you say it?

00:04:13.711 --> 00:04:14.420
- No, no, you a beast.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.506
But sayin’ that—but look—
- But you bein’ judgmental!

00:04:16.506 --> 00:04:19.217
- Bruh, just cuz you a big football player
from Mississippi don’t mean you can’t

00:04:19.217 --> 00:04:20.134
mispronounce a word.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.386
- It’s a good point.

00:04:21.386 --> 00:04:23.054
- Are you Johnathan Abram?

00:04:23.054 --> 00:04:25.348
- Wait, what? Oh, s--t, man.

00:04:25.348 --> 00:04:26.266
- I think he s--t himself.

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:26.641
- What did you do?!

00:04:26.641 --> 00:04:27.892
- Man, you—

00:04:27.892 --> 00:04:28.351
- How are we—

00:04:28.351 --> 00:04:29.769
- What did he say to you?!
- How are we blind?

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.478
- Just lookin’ at him, man!

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:31.980
I remember you from Hard
Knocks, always talkin’.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.107
- So why would you watch the Raiders
if you don’t like the Raiders?

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:36.359
I ain’t gonna lie, I think, like, when the
Raiders play the Dolphins, I’ll be like—cuz

00:04:36.359 --> 00:04:38.111
I’m a Raiders fan—I’ll be
like, “Oh, s--t, that’s a win.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.654
We don’t even need to watch the game.”

00:04:39.654 --> 00:04:42.198
- Yeah, well, you know,
sometimes somebody’s gotta win—

00:04:42.198 --> 00:04:44.575
- And that 4-12 record, I always
know y’all gonna be one of the wins.

00:04:44.575 --> 00:04:45.201
Probably two of them—

00:04:45.201 --> 00:04:47.829
- But 4-12 just makes me think it’s like
Mississippi State all over again or somethin’

00:04:47.829 --> 00:04:49.289
like that, you know what I mean?

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:50.081
- Mississippi State?

00:04:50.081 --> 00:04:50.915
- Yeah, Mississippi State.

00:04:50.915 --> 00:04:52.834
It’s a good junior college football
program, I think, Mississippi State—

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:55.378
- Hold on, now. Stop playin’ with me.

00:04:55.378 --> 00:04:58.006
- It’s a good junior
college football program!

00:04:58.006 --> 00:05:00.008
- Stop playin’ with me.
- I’m not playing at all.

00:05:00.008 --> 00:05:01.301
I think they’re very, very good.

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.427
- It’s good!

00:05:02.427 --> 00:05:03.136
- What good?

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:03.845
- Salmon!

00:05:03.845 --> 00:05:05.888
- What’s up?
- What’s up?

00:05:05.888 --> 00:05:07.432
Let’s do it!

00:05:07.432 --> 00:05:10.935
- Who made the L silent? Who? Who made it?
- The English language!

00:05:10.935 --> 00:05:11.728
- The English language!

00:05:11.728 --> 00:05:12.854
- Who made English?!

00:05:12.854 --> 00:05:13.896
It’s like sayin’, “Tomato, tomat-oh.”

00:05:13.896 --> 00:05:15.857
- Are we gonna be—
- Don’t nobody say “tomat-oh,” bruh.

00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:17.775
- Why?
- Timeout.

00:05:17.775 --> 00:05:20.028
- [Laughing]

00:05:20.028 --> 00:05:22.488
- Ain’t no love. Ain’t no love.

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:25.450
Give him—if he put on a Raiders
hat, I’ll show him some love.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:26.909
Come to the next game.

00:05:26.909 --> 00:05:28.328
- Dress in silver and black.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:31.247
- If you get me tickets, I
have a jersey—I’d be there.

00:05:31.247 --> 00:05:33.875
- Deal.
- Are you serious?
- Let’s do it.

00:05:33.875 --> 00:05:35.918
- I got two tickets, deal.
- We just, we just switched fan allegiance?

00:05:35.918 --> 00:05:37.420
It’s happening.
- Just win, baby.

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.213
- Raider Nation just grew by one.

00:05:39.213 --> 00:05:40.673
- Screw the Dolphins!
- Screw the Dolphins!

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.425
- Who needs a Dolphin?

00:05:42.425 --> 00:05:45.636
- Just win, baby.
You gotta take that off.

00:05:45.636 --> 00:05:48.681
If we ever see you with that
god-awful orange and green on—

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:51.934
You’re a Raidaaa.
What is he, what is he?

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:54.812
- [Together] : He’s a Raidaaa.

00:05:54.812 --> 00:05:56.522
- We’re here to bring you back.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:57.148
- To the Raiders?

00:05:57.148 --> 00:05:58.316
- We tryna sign you.
- We’re here to bring you back.

00:05:58.316 --> 00:06:00.526
- I’m just lettin’ you know,
like, we finna take off.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:03.529
You know how you get on the flight and they
be like, “The boarding door closing in 10 minutes”?

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.114
- Yeah, yeah.
- It’s closin’.

00:06:05.114 --> 00:06:07.033
You got—you ain’t got much
longer to get on the plane.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:09.494
- I got y’all. I’ll root for you.
- What do you mean?

00:06:09.494 --> 00:06:11.579
- I, I—I got y’all.

00:06:11.579 --> 00:06:13.289
- Wait, you’re now rootin’ for the Raiders?

00:06:13.289 --> 00:06:14.332
- Maaan, yeah.

00:06:14.332 --> 00:06:16.959
- [Cheering]

00:06:16.959 --> 00:06:19.921
- I’ll root for you.
- Ayyy!

00:06:19.921 --> 00:06:21.714
I think today was a successful day.

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:25.468
I think we proved to everybody that
you are the best teammate ever.

00:06:25.468 --> 00:06:26.969
- Ever.
- Nobody can talk trash on your team.

00:06:26.969 --> 00:06:29.722
- We are the best team.
- We grew Raider Nation by three.

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:32.058
Got three new fans back in the fold.

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:34.185
- Hey, one by one, baby.
We gettin’ better.

00:06:34.185 --> 00:06:36.312
You got somethin’ to say about
the Raiders, just be aware, 

00:06:36.312 --> 00:06:37.855
we might be hidin’ in your room.

00:06:37.855 --> 00:06:38.773
- What?!

